---
title: Tool approval lifecycle
---
%% Source of truth: packages/harness/src/felix/approvals/store.py and
%% approvals/interrupt.py; the wrapper is builder.py:apply_approvals.
stateDiagram-v2
    accTitle: States a tool-call approval moves through
    accDescr: When a manifest's approval rule matches a tool call, the wrapper looks for an existing approved grant for the same call signature before creating anything. A grant marked one_shot is searched with unconsumed_only, so it authorises exactly one call; without that flag one approval would authorise unlimited replays until it expired. Denied and expired are both terminal, and neither can become approved. Consuming a grant is a single conditional UPDATE, so two concurrent identical calls cannot both spend it. An approver may substitute the call's arguments when deciding, and the tool then runs with the edited ones.

    [*] --> Matched : approval rule matches the tool call
    Matched --> Approved : find_approved returns a live grant
    Matched --> Pending : no grant, create_pending writes a row

    Pending --> Approved : decide(approved), optionally with edited_args
    Pending --> Denied : POST /approvals decide(denied)
    Pending --> Expired : expires_at passes

    Approved --> Consumed : one_shot grant spent by this call
    Approved --> Approved : reusable grant, replayed until expiry
    Approved --> Expired : expires_at passes

    Consumed --> [*] : tool executes once
    Denied --> [*] : deny_output returned to the model
    Expired --> [*] : treated as no grant, re-prompts

    note right of Pending
        The run is suspended here.
        Nothing executes until a
        human decides or it expires.
    end note
